{
  "0": "Change only training strategy: retain the existing optimizer and initial learning rate, but halve the learning rate after two validation checks without HR@10 improvement, with a floor of 0.125 times the initial rate. Keep batch size, dropout, weight decay, stopping policy and the 200-epoch cap unchanged. Smaller late updates may reduce the observed validation oscillation. Apply to all four categories with seeds unchanged.",
  "1": "Change only sequence modeling: cap each causal input history at its latest 30 interactions, preserving chronological order and using identical truncation during training and prediction. Keep target examples, features, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged. A shorter context may suppress stale preferences and reduce recurrent computation across all four categories.",
  "2": "Change only network architecture: apply learned LayerNorm to the GRU candidate-state preactivation before its tanh, leaving reset and update gates unchanged. Preserve recurrent depth, hidden width, embeddings, history selection, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Stabilizing candidate-state scale may improve recurrent optimization with little added computation. Train one model per category and update the predictor writer to reconstruct this GRU cell.",
  "3": "Change only embedding representation: normalize each nonpadding input item embedding by its root-mean-square magnitude using epsilon 1e-6, followed by one jointly learned scalar gain initialized to 1. Keep padding zero and preserve output embeddings, scoring, GRU topology, history policy, loss and optimizer. Controlling input magnitude may improve sparse-item generalization across all four categories. Reproduce normalization in the predictor writer."
}
